        "original_id": "3bad4a54-800f-57a2-be25-33587fc3ad3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Conrad, Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington, Sam Waterston, David Soul, Frank M. Robinson, Thomas N. Scortia\n- Products: Baa Baa Black Sheep, Black Sheep Squadron, The Fifth Missile, The Gold Crew\n- Organizations: United States Marine Corps\n- Roles: combat pilot, fighter ace\n- Topics: World War II, American ballistic missile submarines\n\nFacts:\n- Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington was born on December 4, 1912.\n- Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington was an American combat pilot and a United States Marine Corps fighter ace during World War II.\n- Robert Conrad portrayed World War II ace Pappy Boyington in the television series Baa Baa Black Sheep, which was later syndicated as Black Sheep Squadron.\n- The Fifth Missile is a 1986 TV movie starring Robert Conrad, Sam Waterston, and David Soul.\n- The Fifth Missile is about an American ballistic missile submarine.\n- The Fifth Missile was based on the novel The Gold Crew by Frank M. Robinson and Thomas N. Scortia.\n- Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington died on January 11, 1988.",
